---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How do I work out my pool volume?',
    a: 'Multiply surface area by average depth to get cubic feet, then multiply by 7.48 for US gallons. For a rectangular pool that is length × width × average depth × 7.48. The calculator does this for rectangular, round, oval, and freeform pools.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is my pool’s average depth?',
    a: 'Add the shallow-end depth to the deep-end depth and divide by two. A pool that is 3 feet at the steps and 8 feet at the drain averages 5.5 feet. If your pool has a long flat shallow shelf before it drops off, the true average sits a little shallower than that.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How accurate is the calculator?',
    a: 'For rectangular, round, and oval pools the geometry is exact, so the answer is only as good as your measurements. Freeform and kidney shapes use the standard 0.85 area factor and usually land within about 5%. Steps, benches, and tanning ledges are not subtracted, so a pool with a big ledge will read slightly high.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you measure my pool from satellite imagery?',
    a: 'Not yet. That is the tool we are building, and it is not live. For now the calculator needs dimensions you measure yourself. Join the waitlist and we will email you when the satellite version is ready.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it cost anything?',
    a: 'No. The calculator is free, needs no account, and works on a phone.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Should I measure the water or the deck?',
    a: 'Measure the water at the waterline. Including the coping or deck can add several hundred gallons to the result on a mid-size pool, which is enough to throw off chemical dosing.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="bg-navy-50 py-24">
  <div class="container-page">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="mt-6 text-3xl sm:text-4xl">Common questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-4">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-navy-100 bg-white px-6 py-5 transition-shadow open:shadow-md">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-navy-900">
              {faq.q}
              <svg
                class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-blue-500 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2.5"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              >
                <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy-500">{faq.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
